// ---------- NAMUNAVIY INSHOLAR (Band 7+): har paragraf nima ish qilishini tushuntirib ----------
IELTS.models.push(
  { id: "m_health", k: "w2", type: "Opinion: agree or disagree",
    q: "Some people think that the best way to improve public health is to increase the number of sports facilities. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
    paras: [
      ["Introduction", "It is often argued that building more sports facilities, such as gyms, swimming pools and football pitches, is the most effective way to make a population healthier. While I accept that these facilities can play a useful role, I disagree that they are the best solution, because poor health is caused mainly by diet and daily habits that new buildings alone cannot change.",
        "1-gap savolni boshqa so'zlar bilan qayta aytadi (paraphrase). 2-gap aniq pozitsiya: qisman qo'shilaman, lekin asosan qarshiman. Imtihonchi fikringni birinchi paragrafdanoq ko'rishi kerak."],
      ["Body 1", "Admittedly, better access to sports facilities can encourage some people to exercise more. In many neighbourhoods, there is simply nowhere safe or affordable to play sport, so young people spend their free time indoors. A new public pool or an outdoor gym can give them an alternative, and when facilities are free or cheap, families on low incomes are more likely to use them. In this sense, investment in sport can certainly bring benefits.",
        "\"Admittedly\" bilan qarshi tomonning kuchli tomonini tan oladi: bu Band 7 belgisi. Paragraf bitta g'oya atrofida: sabab, tushuntirish, natija."],
      ["Body 2", "However, the people who most need to improve their health are often the least likely to visit a gym. Many adults work long hours and feel too tired to exercise in the evening, and a new sports centre will not change that. Moreover, the main causes of illnesses such as diabetes and heart disease are unhealthy food, smoking and a lack of everyday movement. For example, a person who eats fast food every day will not become healthy by playing football once a week. Measures such as taxes on sugary drinks, clear food labels and health education in schools are therefore likely to have a much greater effect.",
        "Asosiy argument eng uzun paragrafda. \"However\" burilish, \"Moreover\" qo'shimcha sabab, \"For example\" aniq misol, \"therefore\" xulosa. Muqobil yechim ham taklif qilingan."],
      ["Conclusion", "In conclusion, although sports facilities can help some people to become more active, I do not believe they are the best way to improve public health. Governments would achieve more by tackling the causes of poor health, especially diet and daily habits, and by treating sports facilities as only one part of a wider strategy.",
        "Xulosa fikrni boshqa so'zlar bilan takrorlaydi. Yangi g'oya yo'q. 2 gap yetarli."],
    ],
    phr: ["It is often argued that ...", "While I accept that ..., I disagree that ...", "Admittedly, ...", "In this sense, ...", "However, the people who most need ... are often the least likely to ...", "Moreover, ...", "For example, ...", "... are therefore likely to have a much greater effect.", "In conclusion, although ..., I do not believe ..."] },
  { id: "m_phones", k: "w2", type: "Discuss both views and give your opinion",
    q: "Some people believe that children should be allowed to use smartphones from an early age, while others think this is harmful. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.",
    paras: [
      ["Introduction", "Smartphones have become part of everyday life, and many parents now face the question of when their children should have one. Some argue that early access to these devices is useful, while others believe it does more harm than good. In my view, young children should have only limited and supervised use of smartphones.",
        "Mavzuga kirish, ikkala fikrni bitta gapda aytish, keyin o'z fikri. \"Discuss both views\" savolida ham fikringni kirishda ayt."],
      ["Body 1", "Those who support early smartphone use point out that technology is an essential part of the modern world. Children who learn to use digital tools early may find it easier to study and work in the future. In addition, educational apps can make learning more enjoyable; for instance, many children learn basic English words through games and videos. Parents also feel safer when they can contact their children at any time.",
        "Birinchi fikr: \"Those who support ... point out that\" bilan boshlanadi. Uchta sabab: kelajak, ta'lim, xavfsizlik. Har biriga qisqa tushuntirish."],
      ["Body 2", "On the other hand, there are serious concerns about the effects of smartphones on young minds. Spending hours on a screen can reduce the time children spend playing outside, reading or talking to their families, which are all important for their development. Furthermore, social media and online games are designed to keep users on their phones for as long as possible, and children are far less able than adults to control this. Some studies have also linked heavy screen use to poor sleep and difficulties with concentration.",
        "Ikkinchi fikr \"On the other hand\" bilan. Muallif shu tomonda, shuning uchun bu paragraf kuchliroq. \"which are all important for ...\" murakkab gap namunasi."],
      ["Conclusion", "In conclusion, while smartphones can offer educational benefits and peace of mind for parents, the risks for young children are significant. I therefore believe that children should use these devices only for short periods, with clear rules set by their parents, until they are old enough to use them responsibly.",
        "Ikkala tomonni bitta gapda yig'ib, fikrni aniq takrorlaydi va amaliy yechim beradi."],
    ],
    phr: ["Some argue that ..., while others believe ...", "In my view, ...", "Those who support ... point out that ...", "In addition, ...", "for instance, ...", "On the other hand, there are serious concerns about ...", "Furthermore, ...", "Some studies have also linked ... to ...", "I therefore believe that ..."] },
  { id: "m_housing", k: "w2", type: "Problems and solutions",
    q: "In many cities, the cost of housing is rising quickly. What problems does this cause, and what solutions can you suggest?",
    paras: [
      ["Introduction", "In many cities around the world, the price of buying or renting a home has risen much faster than people's incomes. This trend creates serious problems for individuals and for society, but there are several measures that governments could take to deal with it.",
        "Muammoni qayta aytadi va insho tuzilishini ko'rsatadi: avval muammolar, keyin yechimlar. Bu turdagi savolda shaxsiy fikr shart emas."],
      ["Body 1", "The most obvious problem is that ordinary workers, such as nurses, teachers and shop assistants, can no longer afford to live near their workplaces. As a result, they are forced to move to the edges of cities and spend hours travelling every day, which leaves them less time for their families and increases traffic and pollution. High housing costs also affect young people, who often have to delay getting married or starting a family because they cannot afford a home of their own.",
        "Muammolar paragrafi: \"The most obvious problem is that\" + natija zanjiri (As a result, ..., which ...). Kim zarar ko'rishi aniq ko'rsatilgan."],
      ["Body 2", "To address this issue, governments could, first of all, invest in building more affordable homes, either directly or by giving incentives to private companies. Secondly, rules could be introduced to limit how quickly rents can rise, protecting tenants from sudden increases. Finally, improving public transport would allow people to live further from city centres without spending too much time and money on travel. Cities such as Vienna, where a large share of housing is owned or supported by the city, show that such policies can keep homes affordable.",
        "Yechimlar: first of all, Secondly, Finally. Har yechim qanday ishlashini tushuntiradi. Oxirida haqiqiy shahar misoli: inshoni ishonchli qiladi."],
      ["Conclusion", "In conclusion, rising housing costs push workers away from city centres and make life harder for young people. A combination of affordable housing programmes, rent controls and better transport offers the best chance of solving this problem.",
        "Muammo ham, yechim ham bittadan gapda yig'ilgan."],
    ],
    phr: ["This trend creates serious problems for ...", "The most obvious problem is that ...", "As a result, ...", "..., which leaves them less time for ...", "To address this issue, ... could, first of all, ...", "Secondly, ...", "Finally, ...", "Cities such as ... show that ...", "A combination of ... offers the best chance of ..."] },
  { id: "m_hours", k: "w1", type: "Task 1: line graph",
    q: "The graph below shows the average number of hours per week that young people aged 16 to 24 in one country spent on four activities between 2005 and 2020.",
    chart: { title: "Weekly hours spent on four activities (ages 16–24)", kind: "line", unit: "hours per week", cats: ["2005", "2010", "2015", "2020"],
      series: [{ n: "Watching TV", v: [18, 15, 10, 6] }, { n: "Social media", v: [2, 6, 12, 17] }, { n: "Video games", v: [5, 7, 9, 11] }, { n: "Reading", v: [6, 5, 4, 4] }] },
    paras: [
      ["Introduction", "The line graph illustrates how many hours a week young people aged between 16 and 24 in one country spent on four different activities from 2005 to 2020.",
        "Savolni ko'chirmasdan qayta yozadi: shows → illustrates, aged 16 to 24 → aged between 16 and 24."],
      ["Overview", "Overall, the time spent watching television fell sharply, while social media use rose dramatically and became the most popular activity by the end of the period. Video games also gained popularity, whereas reading declined slightly.",
        "Eng muhim paragraf: raqamsiz, faqat asosiy tendensiyalar. Overview bo'lmasa Task Achievement 5 dan oshmaydi."],
      ["Details 1", "In 2005, young people watched television for 18 hours a week, far more than any other activity. However, this figure dropped steadily over the following fifteen years, reaching just 6 hours in 2020, a third of its original level. Reading followed a similar but much smaller downward trend, falling from 6 hours to 4.",
        "Kamaygan ikki faoliyat bitta paragrafda: guruhlash. Raqamlar aniq, fe'llar xilma-xil: dropped, reaching, falling."],
      ["Details 2", "By contrast, social media accounted for only 2 hours a week in 2005, but this rose rapidly to 12 hours in 2015 and to 17 hours in 2020, overtaking television at some point between 2010 and 2015. Time spent on video games more than doubled, from 5 to 11 hours a week.",
        "O'sgan faoliyatlar ikkinchi paragrafda. \"By contrast\" bog'laydi. Kesishgan nuqta (overtaking) ham ko'rsatilgan. Shaxsiy fikr yo'q."],
    ],
    phr: ["The line graph illustrates how ...", "Overall, ...", "fell sharply / rose dramatically", "far more than any other ...", "this figure dropped steadily", "reaching just ... in ...", "followed a similar but much smaller downward trend", "By contrast, ...", "more than doubled", "overtaking ... at some point between ... and ..."] },
);
